# DuelMasterBattle build execution

- Work from `Pack/DuelMasterBattle_Build_Pack/AGENT_START_HERE.md`.
- Apply `Pack/DuelMasterBattle_Build_Pack/EXECUTION_AMENDMENTS.md`.
- Resume only from `Pack/DuelMasterBattle_Build_Pack/tracking/progress.json`;
  read its current task card, named contract, repository map and prior receipt.
- The repository map is
  `Pack/DuelMasterBattle_Build_Pack/tracking/repository_map.json` once T001
  creates it. Logical pack paths must be mapped to this checkout.
- Python exclusively owns durable world state in the migrated runtime. Godot
  owns presentation, input, local movement and explicitly leased encounters.
  Never introduce competing live simulations or save writers.
- Preserve compatible existing duel, puzzle, village and test behaviour.
  Fixtures and training use the same authoritative simulation as normal play.
- Run meaningful behavioural checks as well as Godot import checks. Record
  evidence and commit each accepted task.
- Continue through dependency-ready tasks; stop at required human gates or
  after three focused failed repairs with a diagnostic handoff.
- Do not load the full GDD or all task cards unless a concrete ambiguity
  requires it.
- G04 retained-UI repair: follow
  `docs/DuelMasterBattle_G04_Reuse_Repair_Addendum.md` (U01–U08) and the G04
  section of `EXECUTION_AMENDMENTS.md`. Reuse `game_board` + `DmbBattleSim`;
  preserve military menu appearance; observation-led names; shared target
  session. Keep T077 unstarted until Joe clears G04. Traceability:
  `Pack/DuelMasterBattle_Build_Pack/tracking/interaction_traceability.json`.
